// Generated by scripts/sync-legal.mjs from docs/legal - edit those files, not this one.
export const LEGAL_MARKDOWN = {
  terms: "# Solid Connect — Terms of Service\n\n**DRAFT — not reviewed by counsel. See `README.md` in this folder before\nusing this document for anything.**\n\n_Last drafted: 2026-09-13._\n\n## 1. Who this agreement is with\n\nThese Terms of Service (\"Terms\") are an agreement between you and Solid\nConnect Limited (\"Solid Connect\", \"we\", \"us\") governing your use of the\nSolid Connect mobile app and any related services (the \"App\"). By creating\nan account or using the App, you agree to these Terms.\n\n## 2. What Solid Connect is\n\nSolid Connect is a marketplace app that connects **customers** in Accra,\nGhana who need a home-services job done (plumbing, electrical, carpentry,\ncleaning, and similar categories) with **providers** — plumbers,\nelectricians, artisans, and cleaners — who offer those services.\n\n**Solid Connect is a facilitator, not the employer of providers and not the\nperformer of any service.** We provide the app, the matching, the chat, the\nescrow/payment flow, and the review system. The actual work is a contract\ndirectly between the customer and the provider. We are not a party to that\nwork contract and do not guarantee its outcome, though we do provide the\nverification, dispute, and refund mechanisms described below to make that\ntrust real rather than assumed.\n\nOne account can hold both a customer role and a provider role; you can\nswitch between them at any time in the app.\n\n## 3. Eligibility and accounts\n\n- You must be at least 18 years old to create an account.\n- You must provide accurate information (name, phone number, email, area)\n  and keep it up to date. Account recovery, support, and dispute handling\n  all depend on this being correct.\n- You are responsible for anything that happens under your account. Tell us\n  immediately (see Section 11) if you believe your account has been\n  compromised.\n- One person may not hold more than one account. We may merge, suspend, or\n  remove accounts that violate this.\n\n## 4. Provider verification\n\nProviders on Solid Connect go through a staged verification process before\nthey can carry certain trust marks in the app:\n\n| Level | What it means |\n|---|---|\n| Registered | Signed up, no documents reviewed yet |\n| Identity verified | Government-issued ID reviewed and approved by Solid Connect |\n| Profession verified | Trade credentials/experience reviewed and approved |\n| Experience verified | A track record of completed jobs on the platform |\n| Solid Connect Verified | The highest mark — all of the above |\n\nVerification is performed by Solid Connect's admin team based on documents\na provider submits. **Verification is not a guarantee of the provider's\nwork quality or a certification of professional competence** — for\nregulated trades, you should independently confirm any license the law\nrequires (see Section 9). Verification can be revoked if we later find the\nsubmitted information was false or the provider's conduct warrants it.\n\n## 5. Posting a job and getting matched\n\n- Customers describe the job, its category, and location; Solid Connect\n  matches nearby, relevant providers using the location and category you\n  provide.\n- A provider who responds gives you a quote. You choose whether to accept\n  it. Accepting a quote creates a job and a payment held by Solid Connect\n  (see Section 7) — it does **not** create an employment relationship\n  between you and the provider, or between the provider and Solid Connect.\n- Once a job is accepted, in-app chat, progress tracking, and (for the\n  duration the job is active) each party's live location become available\n  to the other party, to make coordinating the job easier and more\n  accountable. Location sharing is foreground-only, requires your\n  permission, and is deleted the moment the job completes — see\n  `privacy-policy.md`.\n\n## 6. Job completion and confirmation\n\n- The provider marks the job as done when they've finished the work.\n- The customer then confirms completion in the app. Confirming releases the\n  held payment (see Section 7) and unlocks the ability to leave a review.\n- If something is wrong with the completed work, do not confirm — open a\n  dispute instead (see `refund-dispute-policy.md`).\n\n## 7. Payments and commission\n\n- When a customer accepts a quote, the agreed price is held by Solid\n  Connect on the customer's behalf until the job is confirmed complete.\n- On confirmation, Solid Connect releases that amount to the provider,\n  minus a commission (the rate shown in the app at the time — see\n  `docs/legal/README.md` for why this isn't a fixed number here).\n- **As of this draft, Solid Connect does not yet process real payments.**\n  Card and mobile money charging is being built; until it is live, any\n  in-app payment status is for tracking purposes only and no real funds\n  move through the app. This section describes the intended mechanics once\n  real payment processing is connected, not the current state.\n\n## 8. Reviews\n\nAfter a job completes, the customer may leave a 1–5 star rating and an\noptional written comment on the provider. Reviews are meant to reflect a\ngenuine, completed job — do not post a review for a job that didn't happen\nthrough the app, and do not offer or accept payment in exchange for a\nreview. Solid Connect may remove a review that violates this or that is\nabusive, and may adjust a provider's aggregate rating accordingly.\n\n## 9. Professional licensing and your own diligence\n\nSome trades (electrical work in particular) may be subject to licensing or\ncertification requirements under Ghanaian law independent of anything Solid\nConnect verifies. **Solid Connect's verification levels are not a\nsubstitute for confirming a provider holds any license the law requires for\ntheir trade.** Customers engaging providers for regulated work should ask\nto see that license directly.\n\n## 10. Conduct\n\nYou agree not to:\n\n- Use the App for anything illegal, fraudulent, or deceptive.\n- Attempt to move a job's communication or payment off-platform to avoid\n  Solid Connect's dispute and refund protections.\n- Harass, threaten, or discriminate against another user.\n- Submit false information during signup, verification, a job, a review, or\n  a dispute.\n- Attempt to access another user's account or Solid Connect's systems\n  without authorization.\n\nSolid Connect may suspend or remove an account for violating this section.\nA suspended account cannot post new jobs, submit new quotes, or otherwise\nuse the marketplace; work already in progress is handled case by case. See\n`provider-agreement.md` for provider-specific conduct terms.\n\n## 11. Contact and account issues\n\nFor account security concerns, disputes you can't resolve through the app,\nor anything else, contact **support@solidconnect.co**.\n\n## 12. Changes to these Terms\n\nWe may update these Terms as the App changes (for example, once real\npayments go live). We'll make a reasonable effort to notify you of material\nchanges before they take effect. Continuing to use the App after a change\ntakes effect means you accept the updated Terms.\n\n## 13. Limitation of liability\n\n_[Placeholder — this section requires counsel input specific to Ghanaian\nlaw before it can be relied on. A facilitator marketplace typically limits\nits liability for the underlying service performed by a third party, but\nthe exact scope, any statutory limits on what can be disclaimed, and\nrequired consumer-protection carve-outs need legal review.]_\n\n## 14. Governing law\n\n_[Placeholder — to be confirmed with counsel; expected to be the laws of\nthe Republic of Ghana given the app's operating market.]_\n",
  privacy: "# Solid Connect — Privacy Policy\n\n**DRAFT — not reviewed by counsel. See `README.md` in this folder before\nusing this document for anything, especially regarding Ghana's Data\nProtection Act, 2012 (Act 843) and Data Protection Commission\nregistration.**\n\n_Last drafted: 2026-09-13._\n\n## 1. What this covers\n\nThis policy describes what personal data Solid Connect collects through the\nApp, why, how long we keep it, and how you can request it be deleted. It\napplies to both customer and provider accounts.\n\n## 2. What we collect\n\n**Account information** (both roles): full name, initials/avatar, phone\nnumber, email address, area/neighborhood, and a profile photo if you add\none.\n\n**Provider-specific information**: your trade category or categories, a\ntagline/bio, portfolio photos of past work, service areas, and availability\nstatus.\n\n**Verification documents** (providers only): government ID and other\ndocuments you submit to be verified, stored in a private storage location\nonly you and Solid Connect's admin team can access — never shown publicly.\n\n**Job content**: the request you post (description, category, photos you\nattach, budget), quotes exchanged, and the resulting job's details (title,\nprice, location label, status, timestamps).\n\n**Chat messages**: messages exchanged with the other party on a job, tied\nto that job's chat thread.\n\n**Live location — while a job is active only**: if you grant permission,\nyour device's foreground location is shared with the other party on that\nspecific job (so a customer can see their provider en route, or vice\nversa). This:\n\n- Is **never** collected in the background — only while the app is open and\n  the job is in an active status.\n- Is **deleted automatically the moment the job is marked complete** — we\n  do not keep a location history.\n- Is visible only to the other party on that job and to Solid Connect's\n  admin team (for support/dispute purposes), never publicly.\n\n**Reviews**: the star rating and any written comment you leave, tied to\nyour name and the job.\n\n**Notifications**: in-app messages we send you about job updates, quotes,\nand (if you opt in) product announcements.\n\n**Payment information**: once real payment processing is connected (see\n`terms-of-service.md` Section 7), the amount, status, and timing of\npayments and payouts tied to your jobs. We do not store your card or mobile\nmoney credentials ourselves — that will be handled by our payment\nprocessor once one is integrated.\n\n**Usage and device information**: a push-notification token if you enable\nnotifications, and standard technical data (device type, app version)\nneeded to make the app work reliably.\n\n## 3. What we don't do\n\n- We do not sell your personal data.\n- We do not show your phone number or email to other users; they see your\n  name, initials/photo, area, and (for providers) trade/rating/reviews.\n- We do not use your live location for anything other than showing it to\n  the other party on an active job, as described above.\n\n## 4. Who can see what\n\n| Data | Visible to |\n|---|---|\n| Name, photo, area, rating, reviews | Any user browsing the marketplace |\n| Phone, email | Only Solid Connect (used for account recovery and, where a job connects two parties, may be shared between them for coordinating the job) |\n| Verification documents | Only you and Solid Connect's admin/verification team |\n| Live job location | Only the other party on that specific job, and Solid Connect's admin team |\n| Chat messages | Only the two parties on that thread, and Solid Connect's admin team (for disputes/support) |\n| Payment/payout details | You, and Solid Connect's admin/finance team |\n\n## 5. How long we keep it\n\n- **Live location**: deleted immediately on job completion (see Section 2).\n- **Verification documents**: kept for as long as your account is verified\n  or under review, and for a reasonable period after in case a dispute or\n  regulatory question arises about that verification.\n- **Job, chat, review, and payment records**: kept for the life of your\n  account, since they form the accountability history the whole trust model\n  depends on (a provider's rating and job history need to persist to mean\n  anything).\n- **Account information**: kept until you request deletion (Section 6) or\n  your account is removed for a Terms violation.\n\n## 6. Your rights and deleting your account\n\nYou can request account deletion by contacting **support@solidconnect.co**.\nWhen you do:\n\n- Your account information, verification documents, and any personally\n  identifying profile details are removed.\n- Job, payment, and dispute records tied to jobs with **other** users may\n  be retained in an anonymized or minimally-identifying form, since those\n  other users' own accountability history depends on the job having\n  happened — this mirrors how the provider rating/job-count system works\n  today (removing a review recalculates the aggregate rather than just\n  disappearing).\n\n_[Placeholder — the exact mechanics of \"anonymized retention\" above need to\nbe defined precisely and checked against Act 843's data-subject rights\nbefore this policy is finalized; this draft states the intent, not a\nguaranteed technical implementation.]_\n\n## 7. Data storage and security\n\nYour data is stored in Supabase (Postgres), a third-party infrastructure\nprovider, with row-level security policies restricting who can read what —\nfor example, only you and an admin can read your verification documents;\nonly the two parties on a job (and admins) can read that job's live\nlocation or chat.\n\n_[Placeholder — needs a statement on where Supabase's servers are located\n(data residency), whether that satisfies Act 843's cross-border transfer\nrequirements if data leaves Ghana, and Solid Connect's Data Protection\nCommission registration status.]_\n\n## 8. Children\n\nThe App is not intended for anyone under 18. We do not knowingly collect\ndata from children.\n\n## 9. Changes to this policy\n\nWe may update this policy as the App changes. We'll make a reasonable\neffort to notify you of material changes before they take effect.\n\n## 10. Contact\n\nQuestions about this policy or your data: **support@solidconnect.co**.\n\n_[Placeholder — Act 843 may require a named Data Protection Officer and\ntheir contact details, and formal registration with the Data Protection\nCommission before this app processes personal data at any real scale.]_\n",
  refunds: "# Solid Connect — Refund & Dispute Policy\n\n**DRAFT — not reviewed by counsel. See `README.md` in this folder before\nusing this document for anything.** This document describes mechanics that\nexist today in the admin panel (`admin/app/(protected)/disputes`,\n`payments`, `payouts`) applied to a payment flow that is not yet live (see\nSection 1) — read it as the intended policy, not a description of money\nthat has actually moved.\n\n_Last drafted: 2026-09-13._\n\n## 1. How payment escrow works (once live)\n\nWhen a customer accepts a provider's quote, the agreed price is **held by\nSolid Connect**, not paid to the provider yet. It stays held while the job\nis in progress. When the customer confirms the job complete, Solid Connect\nreleases the held amount to the provider, minus commission.\n\n**As of this draft, this is not yet connected to a real payment\ngateway** — no real money is charged or held today. This policy describes\nwhat happens once it is.\n\n## 2. Opening a dispute\n\nIf something is wrong with a job — instead of confirming it complete — a\ncustomer can open a dispute from that job in the App, choosing a reason:\n\n- **Not completed** — the provider didn't finish, or didn't show up to\n  finish, the agreed work.\n- **Poor quality** — the work was completed but doesn't meet a reasonable\n  standard for what was agreed.\n- **Overcharged** — the amount doesn't match what was agreed.\n- **No-show** — the provider never arrived.\n- **Other** — anything not covered above, described in your own words.\n\nA dispute needs a description of what happened. You must open a dispute\nwithin **48 hours of the job being marked complete** — the App enforces\nthis window; past it, the dispute screen shows that filing has closed\nand points you to support instead. A job that hasn't been marked\ncomplete yet has no window - you can still dispute a no-show or an\nin-progress problem.\n\n## 3. What happens after you open one\n\n- The payment tied to that job stays held (not released to the provider)\n  while the dispute is open.\n- Solid Connect's admin team reviews the evidence available on the job:\n  the full status timeline, the chat transcript between you and the\n  provider, and any photos attached to the original request.\n- The admin team resolves the dispute with a written explanation of the\n  outcome, and — where warranted — refunds the held payment back to you\n  instead of releasing it to the provider.\n- If the payment had already been released and paid out to the provider\n  before the dispute was raised, a refund at that point is a direct\n  conversation between Solid Connect and the provider, not an automatic\n  reversal — see `provider-agreement.md` Section 6.\n\n## 4. What a resolution looks like\n\nEvery dispute resolution includes a plain-language note explaining the\noutcome — not just \"approved\" or \"denied\". You can see this note in the\nApp once your dispute is resolved. Possible outcomes:\n\n- **Refunded**: the held payment is returned to you.\n- **Released to provider**: the admin team found the work was\n  satisfactorily completed as agreed; the payment is released normally.\n- **Partial refund**: part of the held payment is returned to you, and\n  the provider is still paid the remainder - used when the work was\n  partly done, or partly met what was agreed.\n\n## 5. If you disagree with a resolution\n\nContact **support@solidconnect.co** with your job reference and the reason\nyou believe the resolution was wrong. This is a manual escalation, not an\nautomated re-dispute — Solid Connect does not currently have a formal\nappeals process beyond direct support contact.\n\n## 6. Cancelling before a job starts\n\n_[Placeholder — this policy currently covers disputes on an already-\naccepted job. A separate policy for cancelling a request before a provider\nis matched, or cancelling an accepted-but-not-yet-started job, needs to be\nwritten; check `docs/marketplace-mechanics.md` for whether that flow\nalready has agreed rules that just need restating here.]_\n\n## 7. Provider no-shows and repeated issues\n\nA pattern of no-show or poor-quality disputes against the same provider is\nalso a conduct matter under `provider-agreement.md` Section 8, separate\nfrom the refund itself — Solid Connect may suspend a provider's account\nindependent of any individual dispute's resolution.\n",
  providers: "# Solid Connect — Provider Agreement\n\n**DRAFT — not reviewed by counsel. See `README.md` in this folder before\nusing this document for anything.**\n\n_Last drafted: 2026-09-13._\n\nThis agreement supplements the general `terms-of-service.md` with terms\nspecific to using Solid Connect as a provider. Where the two conflict, this\ndocument governs for provider-specific matters.\n\n## 1. You are an independent contractor\n\n**Nothing in this agreement or your use of the App makes you an employee,\nagent, partner, or joint venturer of Solid Connect.** You are an\nindependent business providing services directly to customers you're\nmatched with. You are responsible for your own:\n\n- Taxes and any business registration the law requires for your trade.\n- Tools, materials, and insurance for the work you perform.\n- Compliance with any professional licensing your trade requires (see\n  Section 4).\n\nSolid Connect does not direct how you perform a job, set your working\nhours, or provide you with equipment.\n\n## 2. Getting verified\n\nTo appear as a verified provider, you submit identity and (depending on the\nverification level you're pursuing) professional documents through the\nApp. Solid Connect's admin team reviews these and approves or rejects each\nsubmission, with a reason given if rejected. You may resubmit after\naddressing the reason. See `terms-of-service.md` Section 4 for the level\nstructure.\n\n**Submitting false or altered documents is grounds for immediate account\nsuspension** and may be reported to relevant authorities where the law\nrequires it.\n\n## 3. Categories, service areas, and availability\n\nYou choose which service categories you offer, which neighborhoods/areas\nyou serve, and your availability status (available now, scheduled,\nunavailable, or paused). These directly control which job requests you're\nmatched against — keep them accurate so you're matched with work you\nactually want and can do.\n\n## 4. Professional licensing is your responsibility\n\nSolid Connect's verification confirms what you submitted to us; **it does\nnot certify that you hold every license your trade legally requires**\n(electrical work, for example, often has statutory licensing\nrequirements in Ghana independent of anything Solid Connect checks). You\nare responsible for holding any license the law requires for the work you\naccept, and for being able to show it to a customer who asks.\n\n## 5. Quoting and accepting jobs\n\n- You may quote on a customer's posted request, or accept a request sent\n  directly to you.\n- A quote you submit is an offer at that price; once a customer accepts it,\n  you are agreeing to perform the described job at that price, subject to\n  the customer's payment being held by Solid Connect per the escrow flow\n  in `refund-dispute-policy.md`.\n- If you can no longer do a job you've been matched to, communicate that to\n  the customer through the App as early as possible rather than going\n  silent — repeated no-shows or unresponsiveness are conduct issues under\n  Section 8.\n\n## 6. Getting paid\n\n- When a customer confirms a job complete, Solid Connect releases the held\n  payment to you, minus Solid Connect's commission (the rate shown in the\n  app at the time of the job — see the note in `docs/legal/README.md`).\n- Payout is sent to the mobile money number or bank account you provide in\n  your payout details. **As of this draft, real payment processing is not\n  yet connected** — see `terms-of-service.md` Section 7. This section\n  describes the intended mechanics once it is.\n- If a dispute results in a refund to the customer after you were already\n  paid out, Solid Connect will contact you directly about resolving that —\n  this is not something the App does automatically (see\n  `refund-dispute-policy.md`).\n\n## 7. Reviews and your rating\n\nCustomers rate completed jobs 1–5 stars with an optional comment. Your\ndisplayed rating is the average of all your non-removed reviews. Solid\nConnect may remove a review that violates the review rules in\n`terms-of-service.md` Section 8, which recalculates your rating\naccordingly — removing a bad-faith review is not something you need to\ndispute separately.\n\n## 8. Conduct specific to providers\n\nIn addition to the general conduct rules in `terms-of-service.md` Section\n10, as a provider you agree not to:\n\n- Accept a job you don't intend to complete, or accept work outside a\n  license you're required to hold.\n- Solicit a customer to pay you directly, off-platform, to avoid Solid\n  Connect's commission or escrow protection.\n- Misrepresent your trade, experience, or verification status.\n\nViolating this section can result in suspension. A suspended provider\naccount cannot accept new job requests or submit new quotes; the app\nenforces this the next time you sign in (not instantly mid-session — see\nthe note on suspension enforcement in `docs/roadmap-and-risks.md`).\n\n## 9. Disputes involving your work\n\nIf a customer disputes a job you performed, Solid Connect's admin team\nreviews the evidence (job timeline, chat, any photos) and may resolve it\nwith or without a refund to the customer. See `refund-dispute-policy.md`\nfor the customer-facing version of this process. You will be able to see\nthe dispute's outcome; if you disagree with a resolution, contact\n**support@solidconnect.co**.\n\n## 10. Ending this agreement\n\nYou may stop using the App at any time. Solid Connect may suspend or\nterminate your provider access for a Terms or Provider Agreement\nviolation, with the reason given to you in the App. Payouts already owed\nfor completed, undisputed jobs are not forfeited by account termination.\n\n_[Placeholder — the exact wind-down process for a terminated provider with\nin-progress jobs or pending payouts needs a defined policy before this can\nbe relied on operationally.]_\n",
} as const;
